findings.suggestion:
Replace `forEach(async ...)` with a properly awaited loop so the existing try/catch can catch rejections and the function waits for deletions to complete before returning true. For example:
```ts
try {
  await Promise.all(
    bookingRefsFiltered.map(async (bookingRef) => {
      if (bookingRef.uid) {
        if (bookingRef.type.endsWith("_calendar")) {
          const calendar = await getCalendar(credentialsMap.get(bookingRef.type));
          return calendar?.deleteEvent(bookingRef.uid, builder.calendarEvent);
        } else if (bookingRef.type.endsWith("_video")) {
          return deleteMeeting(credentialsMap.get(bookingRef.type), bookingRef.uid);
        }
      }
    })
  );
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof Error) {
    logger.error(error.message);
  }
}
```
This awaits all deletions in parallel, makes rejections reachable by the catch, and preserves the intent of the original try/catch. Alternatively, use a `for...of` loop with `await` inside if sequential deletion is preferred.

